IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `chr-dates`
IMPORT `chr-core`

-- Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) -- the questions of a person injured in State custody
-- or care, or by a public body, who has a cause of action of their own apart from the Charter.
--
-- SEAT: the injured person (for example a prisoner or someone held by police, a child in out-of-home care, a patient
-- detained under mental health law, a person hurt by a council or a State agency) who has, or may have, a claim in
-- negligence, for false imprisonment or battery, under a statute, or for judicial review. "Is the body that hurt me a
-- public authority?", "Which of my rights did what happened limit?", "Was the act unlawful under the Charter?", "Can I
-- add a Charter ground to my claim?", "Can I get damages for the breach?", "Must the court read the statute in my case
-- compatibly with my rights?", "Must I notify the Attorney-General and the Commission?".
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, numbers, a choice from a list); each calls a rule in chr-core.l4.
-- Judgments the Charter leaves to a court are asked as "if the court finds ..." inputs, never decided. No question takes
-- a DEONTIC or an EVENT; the s 35 duty is built and run inside.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Charter of
-- Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006, Act No. 43/2006, Version No. 015 (1 June 2022), not the authorised
-- version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No
-- part may be reproduced except in accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of
-- 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006: the injured person's questions`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 4 -- is the body that hurt me a public authority`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Is the body or person that injured me (or held me, or cared for me) a "public authority" bound by the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 4? Public officials, Victoria Police, councils, Ministers, statutory bodies with public functions, and private bodies exercising public functions on behalf of the State (such as a private prison operator) are; Parliament, and courts and tribunals except when acting administratively, are not.
GIVEN `kind of body` IS A `Kind of body` @desc What kind of body or person it was: a public official (public servant, department or public entity staff); a body set up by an Act or other statutory provision; Victoria Police; a council, councillor or council staff; a Minister; members of a Parliamentary Committee; Parliament or a person acting in Parliament's proceedings; a court or tribunal; or another body or person not set up by statute (a private company, care provider or contractor)
      `public functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a statutory body or a private body: whether its functions in your case are of a public nature, as a court would find (s 4(2) factors: conferred by statute, connected with government, regulatory, publicly funded, a State-owned company; not conclusive). Running a prison or providing State-funded care often is
      `on behalf of the State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a private body: whether it was exercising those public functions on behalf of the State or a public authority (under contract or otherwise; no agency relationship is needed, and public funding alone is not enough), as a court would find
      `administrative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a court, a tribunal or a Parliamentary Committee: whether it was acting in an administrative capacity (for example issuing a warrant, committal proceedings, listing cases) rather than deciding a case
      `declared to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Charter regulations declare this body to be a public authority (not deposited; answer no if you do not know)
      `declared not to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Charter regulations declare this body not to be a public authority, or not one when exercising the function in your case (not deposited; answer no if you do not know)
GIVETH A `Public authority`
`Is the body that hurt me a public authority` MEANS
    `s 4 -- public authority` `kind of body` `public functions` `on behalf of the State` `administrative capacity` `declared to be` `declared not to be`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Part 2 -- which of my rights did what happened limit`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Did what happened to me limit my right to life under the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 9? Every person has the right to life and the right not to be arbitrarily deprived of life. Whether a failure to protect you (for example in custody or care) limits the right to life is for the court; give its finding. Lists each limb your facts meet; an empty list means none.
GIVEN `life limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find that the act or failure limited your right to life (for example by exposing you, while held or in care, to a real risk to your life that the authority knew or ought to have known of)
      `a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a life was taken (for a claim about a death)
      `arbitrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a life was taken, whether the court would find the deprivation of life arbitrary
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`Did what happened limit my right to life` MEANS
    `s 9 -- limbs limited` `life limited` `a death` `arbitrary`

@export Did what happened to me limit my protection from torture and cruel, inhuman or degrading treatment under the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 10? You must not be tortured, treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading way, or subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment without your full, free and informed consent. Lists each limb your facts meet; an empty list means none.
GIVEN `tortured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find you were subjected to torture
      `cruel or degrading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find you were treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading way
      `medical treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment (for example restraint and sedation, or treatment while detained)
      `consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you gave your full, free and informed consent to it
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`Did what happened limit my protection from cruel treatment` MEANS
    `s 10 -- limbs limited` `tortured` `cruel or degrading` `medical treatment` `consented`

@export Did what happened to me limit my right to privacy and reputation under the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 13? You have the right not to have your privacy, family, home or correspondence unlawfully or arbitrarily interfered with, and not to have your reputation unlawfully attacked. Bodily integrity (for example a strip search or a forced medical procedure) is often argued as privacy; that is for the court. Lists each limb your facts meet; an empty list means none.
GIVEN `interfered with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your privacy, family, home or correspondence was interfered with (for example a search, surveillance, removal of a child, entry to your home, reading your mail)
      `unlawful interference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether a court would find the interference unlawful (not authorised by law)
      `arbitrary interference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether a court would find it arbitrary (capricious, unjust, unreasonable or disproportionate)
      `reputation attacked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your reputation was attacked
      `unlawful attack` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether a court would find the attack unlawful
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`Did what happened limit my right to privacy` MEANS
    `s 13 -- limbs limited` `interfered with` `unlawful interference` `arbitrary interference` `reputation attacked` `unlawful attack`

@export Did my arrest or detention limit my right to liberty and security of person under the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 21(1)-(4), (7), (8)? You must not be arbitrarily arrested or detained, nor deprived of liberty except on grounds and by procedures established by law; you must be told the reason at the time and promptly told of any proceedings; a court you apply to about your detention must decide without delay and order release if the detention is unlawful. Lists each limb your facts meet; an empty list means none.
GIVEN `security limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find the act limited your liberty or security of person in a way not covered by the other questions here
      `arrested or detained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were arrested or detained (held in custody, in a police cell, in a locked ward or facility, or otherwise deprived of liberty)
      `arbitrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether a court would find the arrest or detention arbitrary
      `lawful grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether it was on grounds established by law (a law authorised it)
      `lawful procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether it was carried out in accordance with the procedures established by law
      `told the reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you were told the reason for the arrest or detention at the time it happened
      `proceedings coming` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether proceedings (for example a charge) were to be brought against you
      `promptly told` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you were promptly told about them
      `applied to a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied to a court for a declaration or order about the lawfulness of your detention
      `decided without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the court decided without delay
      `found unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the court found the detention unlawful
      `release ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the court found it unlawful, whether it ordered your release
      `contract imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were imprisoned only because you could not perform a contractual obligation (for example a debt)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`Did my arrest or detention limit my right to liberty` MEANS
    `s 21 -- arrest and detention limbs limited` `security limited` `arrested or detained` `arbitrary` `lawful grounds` `lawful procedures` `told the reason` `proceedings coming` `promptly told` `applied to a court` `decided without delay` `found unlawful` `release ordered` `contract imprisonment`

@export As a person held on a criminal charge or awaiting trial, were my rights under the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 21(5), (6) limited? A person arrested or detained on a criminal charge must be promptly brought before a court, has the right to be tried without unreasonable delay, and must be released if either is not complied with; a person awaiting trial must not be automatically detained in custody. Lists each limb your facts meet; an empty list means none. Only if you were charged.
GIVEN `on a criminal charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were arrested or detained on a criminal charge
      `promptly before a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you were promptly brought before a court, as a court would find
      `tried without unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you were (or are being) brought to trial without unreasonable delay, as a court would find
      `released` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were released
      `awaiting trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were awaiting trial
      `automatically detained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you were detained in custody automatically, without consideration of release on guarantees to attend, as a court would find
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`Were my rights as a person charged limited` MEANS
    `s 21 -- criminal charge limbs limited` `on a criminal charge` `promptly before a court` `tried without unreasonable delay` `released` `awaiting trial` `automatically detained`

@export While I was deprived of liberty, was my right to humane treatment limited under the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 22? All persons deprived of liberty must be treated with humanity and respect for their dignity; a person detained but not convicted must be held apart from convicted prisoners (except where reasonably necessary) and treated as appropriate for an unconvicted person. Lists each limb your facts meet; an empty list means none.
GIVEN `deprived of liberty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were deprived of liberty (in prison, a police cell, a locked ward, a secure care facility or the like)
      `humane treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you were treated with humanity and with respect for your inherent dignity, as a court would find
      `my position` IS A `My position` @desc Your position: accused of an offence and detained; accused and not detained; detained without charge; convicted of an offence; or none of these
      `held with convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were held together with people convicted of offences
      `reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether a court would find that was reasonably necessary
      `treated as unconvicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were treated in a way appropriate for a person who has not been convicted
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`Was my right to humane treatment limited` MEANS
    `s 22 -- limbs limited` `deprived of liberty` `humane treatment` `my position` `held with convicted` `reasonably necessary` `treated as unconvicted`

@export If I was a child in the criminal process, were my rights under the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 23 limited? A child (under 18) who is accused and detained, or detained without charge, must be held apart from all detained adults; an accused child must be brought to trial as quickly as possible; a convicted child must be treated as appropriate for their age. Lists each limb your facts meet; an empty list means none (including if you were 18 or over).
GIVEN `age at the time` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years at the time
      `my position` IS A `My position` @desc Your position: accused of an offence and detained; accused and not detained; detained without charge; convicted of an offence; or none of these
      `held with adults` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were held together with detained adults
      `tried quickly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were accused, whether you were brought to trial as quickly as possible, as a court would find
      `treated for age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were convicted, whether you were treated in a way appropriate for your age, as a court would find
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`Were my rights as a child in the criminal process limited` MEANS
    `s 23 -- limbs limited` `age at the time` `my position` `held with adults` `tried quickly` `treated for age`

@export As a party to a civil proceeding (or a person charged), was my right to a fair hearing limited under the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 24? You have the right to have the proceeding decided by a competent, independent and impartial court or tribunal after a fair and public hearing (the public may be excluded where another law permits), and the judgment must be made public unless a child's best interests or another law otherwise permit. Lists each limb your facts meet; an empty list means none.
GIVEN `a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a party to a civil proceeding, or a person charged with a criminal offence
      `proper court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court or tribunal was competent, independent and impartial, as a court on appeal would find
      `fair hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hearing was fair, as a court on appeal would find
      `public hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hearing was public
      `exclusion permitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the public was excluded from all or part of the hearing, whether a law other than the Charter (for example the Open Courts Act 2013) permitted it
      `judgment public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judgment or decision was made public
      `non-publication permitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was not made public, whether the best interests of a child required that, or a law other than the Charter permitted it
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`Was my right to a fair hearing limited` MEANS
    `s 24 -- limbs limited` `a party` `proper court` `fair hearing` `public hearing` `exclusion permitted` `judgment public` `non-publication permitted`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 38 -- was the act or decision unlawful under the Charter`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Was what the public authority did (or failed to do, or decided) unlawful under the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 38? It is unlawful for a public authority to act incompatibly with a human right, or in making a decision to fail to give proper consideration to a relevant human right; not where a law left it no reasonable choice, not for acts of a private nature, and not for acts or decisions before 1 January 2008. A right is limited compatibly only by a reasonable limit under law that can be demonstrably justified (s 7(2)): that is for the court.
GIVEN `kind of body` IS A `Kind of body` @desc What kind of body or person it was: a public official; a body set up by an Act or other statutory provision; Victoria Police; a council, councillor or council staff; a Minister; members of a Parliamentary Committee; Parliament or a person acting in its proceedings; a court or tribunal; or another body or person not set up by statute
      `public functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a statutory body or a private body: whether its functions in your case are of a public nature, as a court would find
      `on behalf of the State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a private body: whether it was exercising those functions on behalf of the State or a public authority, as a court would find
      `administrative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a court, tribunal or Parliamentary Committee: whether it was acting in an administrative capacity
      `declared to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Charter regulations declare this body to be a public authority (answer no if you do not know)
      `declared not to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Charter regulations declare this body not to be a public authority (answer no if you do not know)
      `day of the act` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act, failure to act or decision, as an ISO date such as 2025-03-14
      `private nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act or decision was of a private nature (for example a public body's purely private dealings), as a court would find
      `no reasonable choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of a statutory provision, a Commonwealth law or other law, the public authority could not reasonably have acted differently or made a different decision
      `religious body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether acting compatibly with the right would have impeded or prevented a religious body from acting in conformity with its religious doctrines, beliefs or principles
      `right limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act limited one of your human rights in Part 2 (ss 8-27; for example life, protection from cruel treatment, privacy, liberty, humane treatment in detention, fair hearing), as a court would find; the Part 2 questions help
      `limit justified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the court would find the limit was imposed under law and is a reasonable limit that can be demonstrably justified in a free and democratic society (s 7(2))
      `a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the public authority made a decision about you (as well as, or instead of, acting)
      `proper consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it made a decision, whether it gave proper consideration to the human rights relevant to it, as a court would find
GIVETH A `Unlawful under s 38`
`Was the act unlawful under the Charter` MEANS
    `s 38 -- unlawful` (`is a public authority` (`s 4 -- public authority` `kind of body` `public functions` `on behalf of the State` `administrative capacity` `declared to be` `declared not to be`)) `day of the act` `private nature` `no reasonable choice` `religious body` `right limited` `limit justified` `a decision` `proper consideration`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 39 -- what the Charter adds to my claim`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Can I add a Charter ground to my claim against a public authority (Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 39(1))? The Charter gives no claim of its own. If, apart from the Charter, you can seek relief or a remedy against the act or decision on the ground that it was unlawful (for example judicial review, or a claim for false imprisonment, battery or negligence), you may seek the same relief on the ground that the act was unlawful under the Charter (s 38).
GIVEN `kind of body` IS A `Kind of body` @desc What kind of body or person it was: a public official; a body set up by an Act or other statutory provision; Victoria Police; a council, councillor or council staff; a Minister; members of a Parliamentary Committee; Parliament or a person acting in its proceedings; a court or tribunal; or another body or person not set up by statute
      `public functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a statutory body or a private body: whether its functions in your case are of a public nature, as a court would find
      `on behalf of the State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a private body: whether it was exercising those functions on behalf of the State or a public authority, as a court would find
      `administrative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a court, tribunal or Parliamentary Committee: whether it was acting in an administrative capacity
      `declared to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Charter regulations declare this body to be a public authority (answer no if you do not know)
      `declared not to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Charter regulations declare this body not to be a public authority (answer no if you do not know)
      `day of the act` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act, failure to act or decision, as an ISO date
      `other claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, apart from the Charter, you can seek relief or a remedy against the act or decision on the ground that it was unlawful (for example judicial review, or a claim in tort such as false imprisonment, battery or negligence), as that other law gives
GIVETH A `A Charter ground`
`Can I add a Charter ground to my claim` MEANS
    `s 39(1) -- a Charter ground` (`is a public authority` (`s 4 -- public authority` `kind of body` `public functions` `on behalf of the State` `administrative capacity` `declared to be` `declared not to be`)) `day of the act` `other claim`

@export Can I be awarded damages because a public authority breached the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) (s 39(3), (4))? No: a person is not entitled to damages because of a breach of the Charter. Any right to damages you have apart from the Charter (for example in negligence or for false imprisonment, or statutory compensation) is not affected.
GIVEN `other damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a right to damages for the act apart from the Charter (for example a claim in negligence, for false imprisonment or battery, or under a compensation statute)
GIVETH A `Damages for a Charter breach`
`Can I get damages for the Charter breach` MEANS
    `s 39(3), (4) -- damages` `other damages`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 32 -- reading the statutes in my case compatibly with my rights`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Must the court read a statute that matters in my claim (for example a limitation period, an immunity, or a power to detain) compatibly with my human rights (Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 32)? So far as it is possible consistently with their purpose, Victorian Acts and subordinate instruments must be interpreted compatibly with human rights, unless an override declaration is in force. An incompatible statute stays valid, and a declaration of inconsistent interpretation gives you no claim.
GIVEN `kind of law` IS A `Kind of law` @desc The law in question: a Victorian Act; a Victorian subordinate instrument (regulations, rules or orders made under a Victorian Act); a Commonwealth Act or instrument; the common law; or the law of another State, a Territory or another country
      `day proceeding commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding was, or will be, commenced, as an ISO date
      `day of reading` IS A DATE @desc The day the court reads the provision (for example the day of the hearing), as an ISO date
      `override made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Parliament has made an override declaration for the provision (or for the Act under which the instrument was made) under s 31
      `override in operation from` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the provision containing the (latest, if re-enacted) override declaration came into operation, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
      `earlier expiry given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether that Act specifies an expiry date earlier than the 5th anniversary
      `earlier expiry` IS A DATE @desc If so, that earlier date, as an ISO date; otherwise any date
GIVETH A `Reading compatibly`
`Must the court read the statute compatibly with my rights` MEANS
    `s 32 -- reading compatibly` `kind of law` `day proceeding commenced` `day of reading` `override made` `override in operation from` `earlier expiry given` `earlier expiry`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 35 -- notifying the Attorney-General and the Commission (only if I raise the Charter in court)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Must I notify the Attorney-General and the Victorian Equal Opportunity and Human Rights Commission because my case raises the Charter (Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 35)? A party must give notice in the prescribed form if a Charter question of law (or a question of interpreting a statute in accordance with the Charter) arises in a Supreme Court or County Court proceeding, or a question is referred to the Supreme Court under s 33; not to the Attorney-General if the State is a party, nor to the Commission if it is a party.
GIVEN `court` IS A `Court` @desc The court: the Supreme Court; the County Court; or another court or tribunal (for example the Magistrates' Court or VCAT)
      `Charter question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a question of law about the application of the Charter, or about interpreting a statute in accordance with the Charter, arises in your proceeding (for example because you rely on s 38 or s 32)
      `referred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a question has been referred to the Supreme Court under s 33
      `State a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State of Victoria is a party to the proceeding
      `Commission a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Victorian Equal Opportunity and Human Rights Commission is a party to the proceeding
GIVETH A `Notices I must give`
`Must I notify the Attorney-General and the Commission` MEANS
    `s 35 -- notices I must give` `court` `Charter question` `referred` `State a party` `Commission a party`

GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court`
      `a Charter question arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `referred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `gave the Attorney-General notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `gave the Commission notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notices given`
`s 35 -- have I given the notices` `the court` `a Charter question arises` `referred` `the State is a party` `the Commission is a party` `gave the Attorney-General notice` `gave the Commission notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 35(1) -- notice is required` `the court` `a Charter question arises` `referred`)
        THEN `yes: s 35 requires no notice from me`
        IF `the State is a party` AND `the Commission is a party`
        THEN `yes: s 35 requires no notice from me`
        IF `the duty is met under` (`s 35(1) -- my duty to notify` `the notices`) `gave the Attorney-General notice` `gave the Commission notice`
        THEN `yes: I have given every notice s 35 requires`
        OTHERWISE `no: I have still to give a notice s 35 requires`
    WHERE
        `the notices` MEANS `s 35 -- notices I must give` `the court` `a Charter question arises` `referred` `the State is a party` `the Commission is a party`

@export Have I given the notices the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) s 35 requires of me as a party? Notice in the prescribed form to the Attorney-General (unless the State is a party) and to the Commission (unless it is a party), where a Charter question arises in the Supreme Court or County Court or a question is referred under s 33. The Act sets no time for it; court rules may.
GIVEN `court` IS A `Court` @desc The court: the Supreme Court; the County Court; or another court or tribunal (for example the Magistrates' Court or VCAT)
      `Charter question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a question of law about the application of the Charter, or about interpreting a statute in accordance with the Charter, arises in your proceeding
      `referred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a question has been referred to the Supreme Court under s 33
      `State a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State of Victoria is a party to the proceeding
      `Commission a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Victorian Equal Opportunity and Human Rights Commission is a party to the proceeding
      `AG notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Attorney-General notice in the prescribed form
      `Commission notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Commission notice in the prescribed form
GIVETH A `Notices given`
`Have I given the notices` MEANS
    `s 35 -- have I given the notices` `court` `Charter question` `referred` `State a party` `Commission a party` `AG notified` `Commission notified`
